  "findings": [
    "GameState ReceiveBeginPlay calls its Ubergraph entry10. That graph obtains/initializes GameStateAccessSubsystem, configures the encryption key, then invokes ClearGameStateVariables at i239.",
    "BP_Logic.ResyncMatch invokes ResetGameVariables(true) at i95. ResetGameVariables invokes GameStateRef.ClearGameStateVariables at i1945 under a Context null-skip gate.",
    "ResetGameVariables isResyncingMatch=true skips the GetDSession/ResetMatchVariable/tagged-actor destruction segment. Both flag branches reach the state-clear call site in the controlled stack model.",
    "ClearGameStateVariables has 54 top-level assignment/call steps. It resets sides and playing side, destruction/deck/turn tables, trigger map, fatigue-next-damage1, HQ ids/references, stop/wait flags, starting side, four faction bytes, bond set, turn number, match flags and side-effect-holder refs.",
    "The native ResyncMatch call at BP_Logic.ResyncMatch i2379 resolves to MatchControllerV2; it is not recursive BP_Logic.ResyncMatch. Its function header carries Native flag. Backend implementation was not executed/certified here.",
    "Managed ReplayRunner.Run constructs a fresh MatchEngine; BotTurnService.RebuildEngine uses a new runner; Replayer uses Prelude or a new self-play engine. These are managed isolation/data-flow observations, not proof of full native reset equivalence.",
    "Managed new GameState defaults Turn=1, ActiveSide=Left, StartingSide=Left and ClientSide=Left, while native clear assigns corresponding zero states. Existing self-play Start writes its selected opening side; imported starting-side producer/order still requires audit.",
    "Native clear SetupSidesInBattle(0,0) also requires separate verification of the managed derived opponent-side/invalid-side representation; no unverified patch made."
  ],
